From: winglm port
Subject: [PATCH] lockscreen: keypad on the second screen when the main one is landscape

A lockscreen in landscape has no room for the PIN keypad (LG Wing in its
T position: 360 logical pixels high). When another built-in screen shows
a lock shield (the Wing swivel screen below the main one), move the keypad
and the unlock button there whenever the unlock box is shown (greeters
show it once a user is picked). The keypad keeps typing into the PIN entry
on the main screen, which switches to the unlock page. Landscape is judged
by the lockscreen size: monitors report their transform only once.

The keypad goes back to the lockscreen before either side is destroyed.
Shields hold a reference on their monitor and the compositor closing a
shield drops it from the manager list: outputs switched off and on
quickly left dangling monitor and shield pointers behind. A monitor gets
at most one shield, so no empty shield can end up on top of the keypad.
---
